# Fingerprints gitleaks must not report. One line per finding, and each line
# pins a single commit, file, rule and line number -- it suppresses that exact
# finding and nothing else. A rule is never disabled and no path is widened;
# a real credential in the same file, or the same string in another commit,
# still fails the scan.
#
# db62fe3 introduced tests/test_integrity.py with a 32-hex fixture key for the
# HMAC signing tests. gitleaks read it as generic-api-key at entropy 3.91,
# which is the correct call on the bytes it saw: a random-looking hex string of
# key length is indistinguishable from a leaked credential. The fixture was
# replaced in the next commit with self-describing ASCII of the same length, so
# the value is absent from the branch tip and from anything that merges. This
# entry covers only the superseded commit, and squash-merging this branch
# retires it: the SHA will not exist on main, and the line can be deleted.
